 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Space-Time Image Formation Model](3268-space-time-image-formation-model.md)
-A method for reconstructing dynamic scenes by representing the object as a 4D density function $h(x, y, z, t)$, discretized into $N_k$ static frames [3268-space-time-image-formation-model.md]. It differs from warp-based methods by treating time as a direct dimension of the density field, allowing for topology changes but potentially suffering from temporal inconsistency [3268-space-time-image-formation-model.md]. Choose this when reconstructing dynamic objects where deformation is complex and topology changes are expected.
