 ### [B-mode Image Reconstruction](5511-b-mode-image-reconstruction.md)
-A differentiable forward model for synthesizing ultrasound B-mode images by solving coupled forward and backward wave amplitude equations across voxel interfaces using a sparse linear system [5511-b-mode-image-reconstruction.md]. It distinguishes itself from standard ray-marching volume rendering by modeling wave physics rather than simple line integrals of density [5511-b-mode-image-reconstruction.md]. Choose this for differentiable ultrasound rendering where acoustic wave propagation physics are critical.
